/// Diffusion Module - Image Generation via Denoising Diffusion
///
/// Implements diffusion-based generative models for text-to-image synthesis.
/// Supports multiple architectures (U-Net, DiT, MMDiT) and schedulers.
///
/// ## Components
///
/// - **types**: Core diffusion types with evidentiality
/// - **vae**: Variational Autoencoder for latent space encoding/decoding
/// - **scheduler**: Noise schedulers (DDPM, DDIM, Euler, DPM-Solver, FlowMatch)
/// - **unet**: U-Net architecture for noise prediction (SD 1.x, SDXL)
/// - **dit**: Diffusion Transformer architecture (PixArt, SD3, Flux)
/// - **text_encoder**: Text encoders for conditioning (CLIP, T5)
/// - **pipeline**: High-level diffusion pipelines
/// - **lora**: LoRA, DreamBooth, and Textual Inversion for fine-tuning
/// - **controlnet**: ControlNet, IP-Adapter, and conditioning methods
/// - **editing**: Inpainting, outpainting, img2img, and upscaling
///
/// ## Evidentiality Usage
///
/// - `data~`: User prompts, input images, external conditioning
/// - `computed!`: Generated latents, denoised outputs, final images
/// - `found?`: Optional parameters, cached intermediate states

pub mod types
pub mod vae
pub mod scheduler
pub mod unet
pub mod dit
pub mod text_encoder
pub mod pipeline
pub mod lora
pub mod controlnet
